# ConnectRPC client

Do not hand-roll `fetch` to `/genius.../Method`. Generate with Buf, then `createClient(Service, transport)`.

## Shared transport (required)

Use the single export from `src/infrastructure/config/transport.ts` for every normal Connect client.

```ts
// ❌ BAD — new transport / URL in a feature or second client module
import { createConnectTransport } from "@connectrpc/connect-web"
const transport = createConnectTransport({
  baseUrl: import.meta.env.VITE_GENIUS_API_URL ?? "http://localhost:8090",
})

// ✅ GOOD
import { createClient } from "@connectrpc/connect"
import { transport } from "@/infrastructure/config/transport.ts"
import { Auth } from "@/gen/genius/auth/v1/auth_pb.ts"

export const authClient = createClient(Auth, transport)
```

That module owns `baseUrl` (`VITE_GENIUS_API_URL`, default `http://localhost:8090`) and app-wide interceptors (`authInterceptor`: bearer except on `Login` / `RefreshToken`, one refresh+retry on `unauthenticated`).

Do not invent a second `createConnectTransport` for product clients. The only intentional bare transport is inside `authInterceptor` for `RefreshToken` (must not re-enter the bearer interceptor).

## Other rules

- Generate from `../new-hires` (`npx buf generate`), or point `buf.gen.yaml` `out` at this app's `src/gen`. Keep `buf.yaml` next to `proto/`.
- `Auth.Register` is in the proto but docs say it is disabled. Invite with authenticated `Users.InviteUser`.
- Connect JSON is camelCase (`fromNode`, `accessToken`), not proto snake_case.
- Streams: `ExecuteToNode`, `DebugRun`, `SubscribeBuildEvents`, `WatchOverview`, `WatchAgentFleet`, `SubscribeEvents`. Docs call `SubscribeBuildEvents` a stub.

Source: `../new-hires/docs/bff-connect-client.md`, `docs/backend/connectrpc.md`.
